  "interpretation": "<ul>\n<li data-start=\"1043\" data-end=\"1113\">\n<p data-start=\"1045\" data-end=\"1069\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><strong data-start=\"1045\" data-end=\"1067\">Normal (&lt;10 mg/L):</strong></span></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1072\" data-end=\"1113\">\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\" data-start=\"1072\" data-end=\"1113\">\n<p data-start=\"1074\" data-end=\"1113\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">No significant inflammatory response.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\" data-start=\"1115\" data-end=\"1254\">\n<p data-start=\"1117\" data-end=\"1164\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><strong data-start=\"1117\" data-end=\"1162\">Mild to Moderate Elevation (10&ndash;200 mg/L):</strong></span></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1167\" data-end=\"1254\">\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\" data-start=\"1167\" data-end=\"1254\">\n<p data-start=\"1169\" data-end=\"1254\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">Seen in <strong data-start=\"1177\" data-end=\"1253\">acute infections, chronic inflammatory diseases (RA, IBD), tissue injury</strong>.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\" data-start=\"1256\" data-end=\"1456\">\n<p data-start=\"1258\" data-end=\"1293\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><strong data-start=\"1258\" data-end=\"1291\">Marked Elevation (&gt;200 mg/L):</strong></span></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1296\" data-end=\"1456\">\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\" data-start=\"1296\" data-end=\"1382\">\n<p data-start=\"1298\" data-end=\"1382\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">Suggests <strong data-start=\"1307\" data-end=\"1379\">severe bacterial/viral infection, trauma, or active autoimmune flare</strong>.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\" data-start=\"1385\" data-end=\"1456\">\n<p data-start=\"1387\" data-end=\"1456\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">Can be used to <strong data-start=\"1402\" data-end=\"1453\">monitor treatment response and disease activity</strong>.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\" data-start=\"1458\" data-end=\"1579\">\n<p data-start=\"1460\" data-end=\"1579\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><strong data-start=\"1460\" data-end=\"1484\">Persistent elevation</strong> may signal <strong data-start=\"1496\" data-end=\"1535\">risk for secondary (AA) amyloidosis</strong>, especially in chronic inflammatory states.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
